{"title":"2003 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Given the areas of the three squares in the figure, what is the area of the interior triangle?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/2/372ee1f13836b7ad774c0aa23e598d4f8b07cbb6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw((0,0)--(-5,12)--(7,17)--(12,5)--(17,5)--(17,0)--(12,0)--(12,-12)--(0,-12)--(0,0)--(12,5)--(12,0)--cycle,linewidth(1)); label(&quot;$25$&quot;,(14.5,1),N); label(&quot;$144$&quot;,(6,-7.5),N); label(&quot;$169$&quot;,(3.5,7),N); [/asy]\" width=\"192\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/d/07d4a247da685400225d1617e4e1141e5942e408.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)}\\ 13 \\qquad\\mathrm{(B)}\\ 30 \\qquad\\mathrm{(C)}\\ 60 \\qquad\\mathrm{(D)}\\ 300 \\qquad\\mathrm{(E)}\\ 1800$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"414\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The sides of the squares are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89f1f44e7b2c1cf015701ebbea88648355b2dc77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5, 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"34\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> for the square with area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/1/dc1603949fc857565a9843087e27d8f7e28f5eac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25, 144$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"53\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/2/3629b1f1f3b22f1a3c927c7ac0467574394f17ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$169$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />, respectively. The legs of the interior triangle are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, so the area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/a/1faaedc7e9b7c05c3ce5988eeb54d6ab77f8c093.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5 \\times 12}{2}=\\boxed{\\mathrm{(B)}\\ 30}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"140\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>(note: the ab/2 area method only works because the converse Pythagorean theorem holds for the triple [<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />]. Therefore, we can find the solution this way because we know the triangle is right ~megaboy6679)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8\" title=\"2003 AMC 8\">2003 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2003 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2003 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2003\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2003 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2003 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2003 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2003 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2003 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2003 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2003 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">6</a>